<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak cen. bank reserves dip to $3.33 bln - Jan 8.</title>
<headline>Slovak cen. bank reserves dip to $3.33 bln - Jan 8.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Monday its hard currency reserves dipped to $3.327 billion as of January 8 from $3.473 billion on December 31.</p>
<p> HARD CURRENCY RESERVES   Jan 8/97    Dec 31/96    Jan 3/96</p>
<p>  NBS reserves ($bln)	3.327	 3.473	  3.424</p>
<p>  Commercial banks	   2.045	 2.321	  1.599</p>
<p>  Entire banking sector    5.372	 5.794	  5.024</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3687</p>
</text>
